		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4678&amp;p=34774#p34774"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Greetings to you! Thank you for the great work you have done. Well, I would like to ask: will there be a continuation in this development on the use of large fonts? I think that you can also increase the width a little (tentatively), because the color screens of the new radio stations allow you to do this. Yes, it will not fit 16-20 characters, but practice shows that this is enough. In the end, you can try, if users don't like it, then it won't take long to curtail this development. But you still need to try. I talk to a lot of people, many have been looking for enlarged fonts for your firmware for a long time, so in my opinion it is very in demand. Thank you for your work!!!</div></blockquote>No.<br><br><span style="text-decoration:underline">There are currently no developers active on this project. </span><br><br><br>IMO. Larger fonts are unlikely ever to be used on this project. <br><br>From the feedback on the forum, most people prefer the fonts at the existing size.  These fonts are the correct size to display the maximum length channel or contact name etc, across the whole width of all displays.<br><br>Any unused vertical space on the UV380 is more likely to be used for other functionality.<br><br>None of the other radios have much ununsed screen area. Even the DM1701 has 8 pixels less vertical height, which limits any additional functionality, and the MD9600, GD77, DM1801 and RD5R have smaller screens.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Dec 18, 2024 9:14 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
