		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4678&amp;p=34714#p34714"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Your thoughts are welcome, but only related to this text <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_wink.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=";-)" title="Wink"></div></blockquote>Thanks for the quick update. I think it's a great idea to have large fonts to take advantage of the UV380's large screen. I think most people would want to use it that way if its possible to made the characters a bit more readable. If it's not too hard to change the fonts, I have a few font suggestions.<br><ul><li>Unibody 8 - Unibody Pro</li></ul><ul><li>Nokia Cellphone (Very similar to the font in OpenGD77. The large letters look great)</li></ul>I couldn't find any screens resolution information for MD-UV380/390. If the resolution is enough, I can also recommend the font that Boeing made for the low resolution screens and the font used in Android.<br><ul><li>B612</li></ul><ul><li>Roboto Mono</li></ul>Have a nice week everyone.<br>73</div></blockquote>The larger text size is not a new font, its a double height render of one of the existing fonts.  <br><br>Its not practical to make more fonts for the firmware.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Mon Dec 16, 2024 9:24 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
